## Conclusion

The experiment compares the performance of the default and tuned Random Forest models. Feature importance is used to identify less influential features, and a feature removal experiment evaluates their effect on model accuracy.

The final conclusion should state whether removing the selected features preserves, improves, or reduces model performance, based on the experimental results.

## How to Run

1. Open the notebook in Google Colab.
2. Run the code cells in order.
3. Review the best hyperparameters and model accuracy.
4. Examine the feature importance chart.
5. Compare the three models and complete the Results section.

No external CSV file is required because the dataset is provided by `scikit-learn`.
